[592.98, "ainst a 59\u201363 GB/s pure-read ceiling. Prefill GEMMs run at about 700 GFLOP/s, Accelerate's best for these\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m     +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m shapes and this layout. Further large gains would need fewer bytes or flops, which the rules forbid.             \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 127 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- **Load is about 95 ms:** roughly 45 ms of transposing plus about 35 ms of unavoidable page faults. A cold page c\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m     +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mache (seen under this machine's memory pressure) can push it to about 0.9 s, and nothing in the program can preven\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m     +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mt that.                                                                                                           \r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m 128 +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m- **Short-context decode attention** (0.1\u20130.4 ms/token) is latency-bound because the weight stream evicts the KV c\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;36;138;61m     +\u001b[38;2;51;51;51mache.                                                                            "]
